&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Chief of Staff you are the right hand of the Managing Director, Germany. You drive the most important cross-functional projects from idea to execution across our B2B2C and B2C sales channels in Germany.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You run the operating rhythm of the German business, build the analyses behind key decisions and act as the MD&#39;s proxy with Sword&#39;s global teams and take on leadership responsibility very quickly. This is a hands-on role with a steep learning curve and a clear path into a leadership position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic projects end to end: E.g.,&amp;nbsp; Optimize existing sales &amp;amp; partnership channels and drive growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the management cadence: weekly business reviews, reporting to Sword leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases and analyses: channel economics, CAC by channel, market sizing, partnership and inorganic growth options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take over high-priority operational topics when needed (e.g., first hires, process set-up, vendor negotiations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the interface to Sword global functions (Finance, Legal, Market Access, People)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years in strategy consulting – experience at McKinsey, BCG or Bain is a plus, as is first experience in a scale-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent structured problem solving; strong in Excel/Sheets and executive communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on execution mindset – comfortable spending half your time on operational delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent German and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: healthcare practice experience, German healthcare knowledge (GKV, DiGA, market access), experience with Krankenkassen or B2B employer partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
